<title>FRANCE: Sanofi wants to sell Nina Ricci-paper.</title>
<headline>Sanofi wants to sell Nina Ricci-paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sanofi, Elf Aquitaine's drugs subsidiary, wants to sell its stake in Nina Ricci perfumes, the newspaper La Tribune said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said Sanofi informed Nina Ricci's staff council last Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Sanofi wants to sell the stake it holds, that is 49.9 percent of the capital, or 56.5 percent indirectly; the rest belonging to Nina Ricci's chairman (Gilles Fuchs) and his family,&quot; the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Sanofi had no immediate comment.</p>
<p>The drug company has itself been the object of speculation since Elf said last year that it was willing to reduce its stake in Sanofi to below 50 percent and find a merger partner for Sanofi.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
